# Demo requests for the order orchestration.
#
# Prerequisites: Azurite running with all three services (VS Code: "Azurite: Start"), then the host: press F5 to debug,
# or run the "run host (no debugger)" task. See AGENTS.md, "Running locally".
# Works with the Visual Studio .http editor (17.12+), Rider, and the VS Code REST Client extension.
#
# Each scenario has two requests:
#   1. POST /api/orders starts an orchestration and returns 202 with management URLs.
#   2. GET the status URL from that response to see the result. Send it again until runtimeStatus is
#      "Completed" or "Failed"; customStatus shows the pipeline's progress while it runs.
#
# Simulated failures (see Orders/OrderActivities.cs):
#   - Payment over 10,000                 -> payment declined, reserved inventory released (compensation)
#   - SKU starting with "OUT-OF-STOCK"    -> unhandled failure: the orchestration fails after 3 attempts (~6s)
#   - Email ending with "@bounce.test"    -> confirmation fails, but the order still completes (ContinueOnError)
#
# Shipping labels come from a simulated carrier HTTP API hosted in this app (Orders/SimulatedCarrierApi.cs).
# It is asynchronous: POST returns 202 + a Location status URL, and the fulfillment sub-orchestration polls
# that URL every 2s (timeout 20s) until the label is ready, which takes about 5s. So a successful order
# takes ~6s to complete; while it polls, customStatus.detail is "FulfillmentOrchestrator".
#   - SKU starting with "OVERSIZED"       -> the carrier rejects the label: payment refunded, inventory released
#   - SKU starting with "SLOW-SHIP"       -> the label is never ready in time: polling times out after 20s
#
# Scenarios 10 and 11 show run leases: CarrierRateSyncOrchestrator allows only one run at a time. Its 10-minute lease is
# renewed every 200s while the sync runs: send { "durationSeconds": 120 } and the host log shows no renewal; the
# lease simply outlasts it. The demo uses the in-memory fake repository, so the lease is shared only within this host.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:7071


### ✅ 1. Happy path: every step runs, including loyalty points
# Expected (after ~6s of label polling): runtimeStatus "Completed", output.status "Completed" with
# reservation, transaction, tracking number (from the carrier's label) and loyaltyPointsAwarded.
# @name happyPath
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1001",
  "customerEmail": "ada@contoso.com",
  "loyaltyMemberId": "LOY-42",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "KEYBOARD-01", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 49.99 },
    { "sku": "MOUSE-07", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 15.00 }
  ]
}

### ✅ 1. Status
GET {{happyPath.response.body.$.statusQueryGetUri}}


### ✅ 2. Happy path without a loyalty member: the loyalty step is skipped
# Expected: runtimeStatus "Completed", output.loyaltyPointsAwarded null,
# customStatus.skippedSteps ["AwardLoyaltyPoints"].
# @name noLoyalty
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1002",
  "customerEmail": "grace@contoso.com",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "MONITOR-27", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 329.00 }
  ]
}

### ✅ 2. Status
GET {{noLoyalty.response.body.$.statusQueryGetUri}}


### ⚠️ 3. Non-critical failure: the confirmation email bounces, the order still completes
# Expected: runtimeStatus "Completed", output.status "Completed",
# output.notes ["SendConfirmation failed: ... bounced."], customStatus.failedSteps ["SendConfirmation"].
# @name emailBounces
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1003",
  "customerEmail": "nobody@bounce.test",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "HEADSET-03", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 89.90 }
  ]
}

### ⚠️ 3. Status
GET {{emailBounces.response.body.$.statusQueryGetUri}}


### ❌ 4. Validation failure: the pipeline stops early (StopIf)
# Expected: runtimeStatus "Completed" (stopping is not a failure), output.status "Rejected",
# output.notes lists the validation errors, customStatus.status "Stopped".
# @name invalidOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1004",
  "customerEmail": "",
  "lines": []
}

### ❌ 4. Status
GET {{invalidOrder.response.body.$.statusQueryGetUri}}


### ❌ 5. Payment declined: compensation releases the reserved inventory
# Expected: runtimeStatus "Completed", output.status "PaymentFailed" with the decline message.
# The host log shows "Released inventory reservation ..." (the compensating activity).
# @name paymentDeclined
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1005",
  "customerEmail": "big.spender@contoso.com",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "SERVER-RACK", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 12500.00 }
  ]
}

### ❌ 5. Status
GET {{paymentDeclined.response.body.$.statusQueryGetUri}}


### ❌ 6. Unhandled failure: an out-of-stock SKU fails the orchestration
# Expected (after ~6s of retries): runtimeStatus "Failed", with failure details mentioning
# "Step 'ReserveInventory' (Activity 'ReserveInventory') failed: SKU 'OUT-OF-STOCK-99' is out of stock.",
# customStatus.status "Failed". Nothing to compensate: no other step had completed besides validation and shipping.
# @name outOfStock
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1006",
  "customerEmail": "linus@contoso.com",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "OUT-OF-STOCK-99", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 10.00 }
  ]
}

### ❌ 6. Status
GET {{outOfStock.response.body.$.statusQueryGetUri}}


### ❌ 7. Polling failure: the carrier rejects the shipping label
# Expected (after ~6s): runtimeStatus "Completed", output.status "FulfillmentFailed", output.notes
# ["Step 'ShippingLabel' (Polling 'RequestShippingLabel') failed: Carrier rejected shipment 'SHP-ORD-1007': ..."].
# The host log shows the compensation: "Refunded ..." then "Released inventory reservation ...".
# @name carrierRejects
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1007",
  "customerEmail": "marie@contoso.com",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "OVERSIZED-SOFA", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 899.00 }
  ]
}

### ❌ 7. Status
GET {{carrierRejects.response.body.$.statusQueryGetUri}}


### ❌ 8. Polling timeout: the carrier never finishes the label in time
# Expected (after ~20s of checks every 2s): runtimeStatus "Completed", output.status "FulfillmentFailed",
# output.notes mentions "still pending after 20 second(s)". Payment refunded and inventory released.
# @name carrierTooSlow
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1008",
  "customerEmail": "alan@contoso.com",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "SLOW-SHIP-PIANO", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 2400.00 }
  ]
}

### ❌ 8. Status
GET {{carrierTooSlow.response.body.$.statusQueryGetUri}}


### ❌ 9. Bad request: rejected by the HTTP starter, no orchestration is started
# Expected: 400 "Request body must be an order with an orderId."
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "missing.id@contoso.com",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "KEYBOARD-01", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 49.99 }
  ]
}


### 🔒 10. Run lease: start a carrier rate sync (takes 20s and holds the lease while it runs)
# Expected: runtimeStatus "Completed", output.status "Completed", output.ratesUpdated 42.
# The host log shows "acquired the run lease" and, at the end, "released the run lease as Completed".
# @name rateSync
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs/carrier-rate-sync
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "durationSeconds": 20
}

### 🔒 10. Status
GET {{rateSync.response.body.$.statusQueryGetUri}}


### 🔒 11. Run lease: start a second sync while the first is running (within 20s of request 10)
# Expected: completes at once without running the sync. runtimeStatus "Completed", output.status "AlreadyRunning",
# output.runningInstanceId is the instance ID of request 10, customStatus.status "Rejected".
# Send it again after request 10 completes: this time it acquires the lease and runs.
# @name rateSyncAgain
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs/carrier-rate-sync

### 🔒 11. Status
GET {{rateSyncAgain.response.body.$.statusQueryGetUri}}


### 🔎 Call the simulated carrier API directly: 202 Accepted with a relative Location header (labels/{jobId})
# @name carrierLabel
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/carrier/labels
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "shipmentId": "SHP-MANUAL-1",
  "orderId": "ORD-MANUAL-1",
  "skus": ["KEYBOARD-01"]
}

### 🔎 Poll the label: 202 for ~5s, then 200 with the label
# Location is relative to the POST URL, so it is resolved against {{baseUrl}}/api/carrier/.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/carrier/{{carrierLabel.response.headers.Location}}


### 🔎 List recent orchestration instances (built-in Durable Functions HTTP API)
GET {{baseUrl}}/runtime/webhooks/durabletask/instances?top=20&showInput=true
